{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And to Benjamin he gave three hundred pieces of silver.</b> The reason for three hundred: corresponding to what the brothers owed for his sale, for ten times thirty shekels, which is the price of a slave, is three hundred. This is from what they said: one who sells his slave to a gentile is penalized up to ten times its value — that is, in the price of the slave, which is thirty." "<b>And five changes of garments.</b> He hinted to him that there was destined to emerge from him Mordecai the righteous, who would go out in five royal garments, as is said (Esther 8:15): ״ומרדכי יצא מלפני המלך בלבוש מלכות תכלת וחור ועטרת זהב גדולה ותכריך בוץ וארגמן״, and this is what is written of him (Esther 2:5): ״בן קיש איש ימיני״, for he was from Benjamin."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:30.580701794Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}